---
const lastUpdated = "September 2026";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Cookie Policy — prodbytes.com</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="back-link" href="/">&larr; Back to all graphics</a>

    <main class="content">
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        This page explains every cookie used on Prodbytes, what it's for,
        and how long it lasts. For our broader data practices, see our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies we set directly</h2>
      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>Cookie</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
          <th>Duration</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>verified</code></td>
          <td>Remembers that you've entered your email, so you're not asked again on future visits or downloads.</td>
          <td>1 year</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <p>
        This cookie contains no personal information itself — just a
        signed token confirming you've previously provided an email. It
        doesn't track you across other websites.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising cookies (Google AdSense)</h2>
      <p>
        This site displays ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its
        advertising partners use cookies to serve ads based on your prior
        visits to this site or other websites, and to measure ad
        performance. We don't control these cookies directly — they're
        set by Google and its partners when an ad loads on this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can see exactly which cookies Google uses and why on
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's own Cookies page</a>,
        and manage your ad personalization settings at
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Most browsers let you block or delete cookies through their
        settings. Blocking the <code>verified</code> cookie just means
        you'll be asked to enter your email again on your next download —
        it won't stop you from using the site. Blocking Google's
        advertising cookies may result in less relevant ads, but won't
        affect your ability to browse or download graphics.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Reach out at <a href="mailto:hello@timdwyer.co">hello@timdwyer.co</a> with anything about this policy.
      </p>
    </main>

    <style>
      body {
        font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
        margin: 0;
        color: #1a1a1a;
      }
      .back-link {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem 0;
        color: #444;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }
      .content {
        max-width: 640px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      .updated {
        color: #777;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        margin-top: -0.5rem;
      }
      h2 {
        margin-top: 2rem;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
      }
      a {
        color: #1a1a1a;
      }
      table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        margin: 1rem 0;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }
      th, td {
        text-align: left;
        padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #e4e4e4;
      }
      th {
        color: #777;
        font-weight: 600;
      }
      code {
        background: #f2f2f2;
        padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-size: 0.85em;
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
